@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p>Effective Date: @DateTime.Now.ToString("MMMM dd, yyyy")</p>

<h2>1. Introduction</h2>
<p>Welcome to Book Nook. Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information.</p>

<h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Personal Information: Name, email, phone number, and address.</li>
    <li>Account Information: Login credentials and transaction history.</li>
    <li>Usage Data: Pages visited, interactions, and IP addresses.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
<ul>
    <li>To provide and improve our services.</li>
    <li>To communicate updates and promotional offers.</li>
    <li>To comply with legal obligations.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Data Security</h2>
<p>We implement security measures to protect your data from unauthorized access, alteration, or disclosure.</p>

<h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
<p>You can request access, correction, or deletion of your personal information at any time.</p>

<h2>6. Contact Us</h2>
<p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, reach out to <a href="mailto:booknook2025@gmail.com">us</a>.</p>



